  "ch3.ctl.c": "Commits C",
  "ch3.cv.aria": "Left side shows Merkle tree structural sharing across the sample repository; right side plots naive vs Git blob counts over commits",
  "ch3.cv.tree": "Sample repo sharing",
  "ch3.cv.new": "new",
  "ch3.cv.shr": "reused",
  "ch3.cv.x": "Commits C",
  "ch3.cv.y": "Cumulative blobs",
  "ch3.cv.naive": "Naive copy",
  "ch3.cv.git": "Git snapshot",
  "ch3.read.new": "New objects this commit",
  "ch3.read.shr": "Unchanged objects reused",
  "ch3.read.naive": "Naive full-copy blobs",
  "ch3.read.git": "Git Merkle-tree blobs",
  "ch3.say": "Editing <code>{path}</code> (depth {depth}) mints only <em>{new}</em> new objects (1 blob + {trees} trees) out of {total}, reusing all {shr} other objects by hash. Over {c} commits on {n} files, Git stores <em>{git}</em> blobs instead of {naive} (saving {save}).",
  "ch3.p4": "Switch the edited path from depth-2 `src/core/hash.js` to root `README.md`: newly created objects drop from 4 down to 2 (1 blob + 1 root tree), while `docs/`, `src/`, and `tests/` sit completely untouched, reusing 11 of 15 objects. One decisive consequence follows: <strong>every tree's hash depends transitively on every single byte beneath it</strong>. Any edit anywhere changes every ancestor tree hash up to the root; conversely, if two commits share the same root tree OID, Git knows in $O(1)$ time that their entire working trees are byte-for-byte identical.",
  "ch3.limit": "The model leaves out: cross-directory rename detection (Git never records moves inside trees; `diff` infers renames heuristically from blob similarity) and packfile compression (chapter 8).",
  "ch4.title": "Commits & the DAG: why history is rewritten by copying, never mutating",
  "toc.ch4": "Commits & the DAG",
  "ch4.law": "A `commit` object is a tiny plain-text block naming a root `tree`, zero or more `parent` hashes, author/committer timestamps, and a message; because hashes lock down every `parent` pointer, `amend` and `rebase` never edit old commits in place—they mint fresh commits and move branch labels.",
  "ch4.p1": "Trees freeze the filesystem at one instant, yet they carry no timeline. What links snapshots into history is the third object type: <strong>commit</strong>. Inspect any commit with `git cat-file -p HEAD` and you see only plain ASCII lines:",
  "ch4.f1": "`tree &lt;oid&gt;`: the root directory snapshot for this revision;",
  "ch4.f2": "`parent &lt;oid&gt;`: zero lines for a root commit, one for a normal commit, two or more for a merge commit;",
  "ch4.f3": "`author` and `committer`: name, email, Unix timestamp, timezone offset;",
  "ch4.f4": "a blank line followed by the commit message.",
  "ch4.p2": "Connecting every commit to its `parent` pointers yields an immutable <strong>directed acyclic graph (DAG)</strong> (see <a href=\"../../algorithms/graph-algorithms/#step0\">Graph Algorithms</a>). Changing a single character in an older commit—even shifting its timestamp by 1 second—changes its hash, which invalidates the `parent` hash stored inside every descendant commit.",
  "dg.dag.cap": "Figure 4. Top: plain-text body of a commit object. Bottom: `git commit --amend` leaves old commit `C2` completely untouched inside `.git/objects/` while writing a brand-new commit `C2'` with the same parent `C1`.",
  "dg.dag.aria": "Diagram: commit object payload (tree, parent, author, committer, message) and DAG showing C2' created alongside orphaned C2 during amend",
  "dg.dag.ct": "tree 07ed5a7...",
  "dg.dag.cp": "parent d60f514...",
  "dg.dag.ca": "author Ada ... 1700000000",
  "dg.dag.cm": "Commit message body",
  "dg.dag.old": "orphaned",
  "dg.dag.ptr": "main",
  "ch4.p3": "That is why \"rewriting history\" (`git commit --amend`, `git rebase`) <strong>never overwrites existing objects</strong>. In our default graph, `C0` hashes to `4d52cce` and `C2` hashes to `fe4abc2`; running `amend` computes a brand-new commit `bfc744d` pointing back to `C1` and moves `main` over to it, while `fe4abc2` stays intact in `.git/objects/`. Try stepping through the graph operations below.",
  "ch4.model.title": "Rewriting History on an Immutable Commit DAG",
  "ch4.model.how": "Click <code>commit</code>, <code>amend</code>, <code>rebase</code>, or <code>merge</code> to watch the DAG and the live <code>HEAD</code> commit byte payload update. Dashed red circles mark older commits left behind in <code>.git/objects/</code> after branch pointers move.",
